# 0002. Start from the house template layers

Status: Accepted

## Context

Every project needs the same agent workflow, CI, security and governance. Rebuilding them per project drifts and wastes the first days of every project.

## Decision

{{ project_name }} starts from `house-template-base`{% for s in stacks %} and `house-template-{{ s }}`{% endfor %}, applied with Copier, each layer with its own answers file (`.copier-answers.<layer>.yml`). Template-owned files are listed in `.github/template-owned/`. Generic improvements go upstream to the template; the weekly template update brings new versions back as a pull request.

## Consequences

- Answers files are never edited by hand; change an answer with `copier update -a <file> --data key=value`.
- A pull request that changes a template-owned file gets a CI warning, to keep improvements flowing upstream.

## Alternatives considered

- Copying files from an existing project: no update path, and drift starts on day one.
- One template repository for all layers: Copier versions a template by its repository's tags, so layers in one repository would share one version line.

## Sources

- Copier, applying multiple templates to the same project: https://copier.readthedocs.io/en/stable/configuring/#applying-multiple-templates-to-the-same-subproject
- Copier, updating a project: https://copier.readthedocs.io/en/stable/updating/
